{!</table>!}

@potus_menu_1876

- @victory_1876
- @defeat_dem_1876
- @disputed_election_1876

@victory_1876
title: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span> win the 1876 election!
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span>: [+ repEVTotal +] electoral votes
view-if: potus_winner = "rep"
on-arrival: {!
    Q.president = Q.Candidate;
    Q.president_party = "rep";
!}

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span> have carried a clear majority. [+ Candidate +] will be the next President of the United States, with no dispute over the outcome.

[? if third_term_bid = 1 and third_term_won = 1 : The third-term question, so feared by the party's managers, did not sink the ticket after all. ?]

@defeat_dem_1876
title: The <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrats**</span> have won the presidency.
subtitle: <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrats**</span>: [+ demEVTotal +] electoral votes
view-if: potus_winner = "dem"
on-arrival: {!
    Q.president = Q.dem_candidate_1876;
    Q.president_party = "dem";
!}

[+ dem_candidate_1876 +] and the <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democratic Party**</span> have carried a clear majority of the electoral vote. For the first time since before the war, a <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrat**</span> will occupy the White House. The Redemption of the South, already well underway in statehouses across the region, now has a friend in Washington.

@disputed_election_1876
view-if: potus_winner = "disputed"
go-to: Disputed

@Disputed
title: Ummmmm...

= A Disputed Election

Neither candidate has secured an undisputed majority. Returning boards in [+ disputed_states_1876 +] have submitted competing sets of electoral votes — one certified by <span style="color: #002765;">**Bourbon Democrat**</span>-aligned officials, one by Republican-appointed returning boards backed by federal troops. Both candidates are claiming victory. The Constitution offers no clear mechanism for resolving a dispute of this kind, and the nation has not faced one before.

How does the administration proceed?

- @fight_for_electors: Press for full federal certification of the disputed Republican electors
- @concede_disputed: Accept the Democratic returning boards' certifications and concede the disputed states
- @broker_compromise: Broker a compromise — the presidency in exchange for the end of Reconstruction

@fight_for_electors
choose-if: occupation >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Federal occupation in the disputed states is too weak to make this claim stick.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.president = Q.Candidate;
    Q.president_party = "rep";
    Q.potus_winner = "rep";
    Q.compromise_1877 = 0;
    Q.whiteL_militancy += 0.12;
    Q.kkk_militancy += 0.08;
    Q.radical_strength += 3;
    Q.dem_relation -= 10;
!}

The administration presses the returning boards to certify the Republican electors in every disputed state, backed by the continued presence of federal troops. [+ Candidate +] takes the presidency, but <span style="color: #002765;">**Bourbon Democrats**</span> across the South call it a stolen election imposed at bayonet-point. Redeemer militias, already organized and armed, treat the outcome as final proof that only force will settle the question of home rule.

@concede_disputed
on-arrival: {!
    Q.president = Q.dem_candidate_1876;
    Q.president_party = "dem";
    Q.potus_winner = "dem";
    Q.compromise_1877 = 0;
    Q.dem_relation += 8;
!}

Rather than contest returning boards openly aligned with armed Redeemer organizations, the administration accepts the Democratic certifications. [+ dem_candidate_1876 +] will be the next President. It avoids a constitutional crisis, but it hands the <span style="color: #002765;">**Bourbon**</span> wing of the Democratic Party exactly the validation it wanted, in exactly the states where the ballot was least free.

@broker_compromise
on-arrival: {!
    Q.president = Q.Candidate;
    Q.president_party = "rep";
    Q.potus_winner = "rep";
    Q.compromise_1877 = 1;
    Q.reconstructionPlanActive = 0;
    Q.occupation = 0;
    Q.South_army_strength = 0;
    Q.whiteL_militancy -= 0.10;
    Q.dem_relation += 5;
    Q.radical_dissent += 20;
    Q.freemen_rep -= 10;
!}

Quiet negotiations produce a bargain: [+ Candidate +] will take the presidency, and in exchange, federal troops will withdraw from the last occupied statehouses in the South. Reconstruction, in any meaningful sense, is over. <span style="color: #002765;">**Bourbon Democrats**</span> get the home rule they have fought a decade for. <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> call it a betrayal of everything the party once stood for. Freedmen across the South understand, correctly, that the federal government has just walked away from them.